<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances fall in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances fell in the week that ended March 26, the Bank of Canada said on Monday.</p>
<p>				    Wk to Mar 26  Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  27.21   +0.728    +1.356</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     7.07   -0.802    +1.128</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	462.43   +0.990    +5.339</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 131.60   +1.000   -31.400</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.94   -0.007    +2.121</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>					   Feb 97     Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p>M1					  68.61	68.63	58.48</p>
<p>M2					 392.19     394.80     386.93</p>
<p>M3					 499.91     497.80     473.39</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 Feb	   Jan</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-19.81	-16.27</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     692.44	685.16</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    105.81	105.23</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
